@ishuagra02 Agreed. Having 1M tokens available doesn’t mean you want 1M tokens in active context.

We just did an episode on the context hygiene practices we use to keep coding agents performant without burning unnecessary tokens.

https://t.co/Ms2J0U2X61

@mattpocockuk 🎯 That's shifting left for agents - preventing errors to be made in the first place.

We talked about this and 3 other emerging practices for building with coding agents in our latest podcast:

https://t.co/8xlLJ7Onnr

@dexhorthy Interesting framing. It made me think about this through the lens of shifting left:

When the same back-pressure signal keeps recurring, you can move it earlier by encoding it in the spec, so the agent doesn't make the mistake in the first place.

